| `template.required_settings` | list of strings | `["tool.pytest.ini_options.tmp_path_retention_policy", "tool.pytest.ini_options.tmp_path_retention_count"]` in keel; absent means no promises | dotted TOML setting names with no blank parts | check_N, beside `template.twins` in the loader-read manifest; no KEYS row | Protects promised settings in both pyproject.toml and pyproject.toml.jinja, even when both siblings lose one. A malformed list produces one check_N error naming this key. The template block is omitted from generated manifests; absence is silent. | discovering downstream omissions: `audit_project.settings_tables` compares the rendered settings | keel maintainers only |
